  <constraints>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-section-8">TEST-MODIFYING override — unconditional FULL rigor + unconditional Step 9.5 quality gates (code-review + adr-check) regardless of default rigor level. Path-check enforcement (FR-B06): any deletion under `tests/integration/{auth,regression,data-mutation,tenant}/**` requires same-PR replacement — N/A here because ArchTests are under `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/` not integration paths, but the spirit applies: DO NOT delete/weaken guard tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-section-6.5">SILENT VIOLATION IS FORBIDDEN. Each fix explicitly cites §6.5 path (A/B/C) in commit message + code comments. Path A (allowlist entry / exception) requires written reason + ADR citation + reviewer approval. Path B (ADR amendment) triggers separate ADR-amendment task — do NOT bundle silently. Path C (pivot to comply) is default when clean.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests-CLAUDE.md">ArchTests are FORCING FUNCTIONS. NEVER weaken, delete, or scope-narrow to make a test pass. If a guard has a scoping bug (e.g., wrongly includes tests/**), surface as separate amendment candidate; do not silently trim it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="provisioning-KV-lifecycle-rule-1">NEVER re-introduce BFF-API-ClientSecret (either casing) under any name. Not directly touched by this task, but reminder: the FR-F1 fix ADDS an allowlist entry for prong-3 ClientSecret usage — do not use this as license to create a new secret.</constraint>
    <constraint source="provisioning-KV-lifecycle-rule-2">NEVER delete Dataverse-ClientSecret or the soft-deleted rollback copies before 2026-11-23 (auth-v4 rollback window). Not touched by this task; reminder only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028-A4">BFF identity is secret-free. `.WithClientSecret(...)` on the BFF identity is a plain A4 violation with no exception. The FR-F1 offender `WorkerDataverseCredentialFactory.cs:213` authenticates as the WORKER's Dataverse identity (a different identity from the BFF), which is why the prong-3 path is a legitimate transitional exception per adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md — but this exception is NARROW: it does NOT extend to BFF identity credential construction anywhere else.</constraint>
    <constraint source="adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution-doc">Owner-approved 2026-08-25 Q7 narrowing: prong 3 applies to `spaarkedev1` and any as-yet-unprovisioned Model 2 stamp; H4 executor MUST NOT provision new Model 2 stamps under this prong until A36-A42 land per Q6. FR-F1 allowlist entry text must reference this scope narrowly, not implicitly extend it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-39-credential-type-seam">The credential-type seam in H3/H4 stays in code (pluggability); the SECRET path may only be selected for a prong-3 unmigrated environment. `WorkerDataverseCredentialFactory` correctly implements this seam — the ArchTest allowlist just needs to acknowledge the site.</constraint>
  </constraints>

